.TH "SKARN-INVENTORY" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.35.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-inventory \- Inventory assistants, MCP servers, guard mode. Free, no
license
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBinventory\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print one inventory record for this machine: per assistant, the completeness
of its session and configuration observation, its declared session store
roots, the client versions observed in a session, its declared and called MCP
server counts, its last activity and session count; per machine, the
configured and effective guard mode. Read\-only and offline; free, no license.
.PP
Print one inventory record for this machine: per assistant, how completely
Skarn could observe its sessions and its configuration, the declared session
store roots, the client versions observed in a session and when, how many MCP
servers its configuration declares by transport and how many its sessions
called in the window, the last activity and the session count; per machine,
the guard mode the configured hooks ask for and the mode the guard runs in. To
build it, inventory reads the session stores, the assistant configuration
files skarn vet reads, the guard configuration layers and the installed
license, all read\-only and offline. A path is written as an anchor such as
~/.claude.json or $COPILOT_HOME/mcp\-config.json, never as its expanded value,
and a user\-named hook file, plugin directory or custom\-tool root as
<custom>. A run with no \-\-project writes no server name and no project name;
with \-\-project, the names of servers called in sessions in scope and of
servers declared in the project\-local configuration of a project root those
sessions recorded are written masked. Versions are observed in a session,
never installed. The record is the same object skarn check \-\-format ndjson
writes as its skarn.inventory line, documented in NDJSON\-CONTRACT.md. Free,
no license; exit 0 on success, 1 on a usage error, 6 when the home directory
cannot be resolved, the \-\-rules pack cannot be loaded or the collection
fails. On exit 6 stdout still carries the record, as a failure record with
event.outcome failure and an error.code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format. json prints the record indented; ndjson prints it as one
skarn.inventory line. One of: json, ndjson. The default is json.
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fIN\fR
Read sessions modified in the last N hours; 0 reads the whole history. The
default is 720.
.TP
\fB\-\-cli\fR \fItool\fR
Read sessions of one tool only, named as check names it; the other assistants
with a session reader are reported as filtered, and their configuration is
still read and counted. A name that matches no session source on this machine
is a usage error.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIlist\fR
Scope to sessions whose project name or root matches an entry of this
comma\-separated list, as check matches it, and write the server and project
names that scope allows.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIlist\fR
Keep only sessions whose recorded user id or email matches an entry of this
comma\-separated list, as check matches it.
.TP
\fB\-\-rules\fR \fIpath\fR
Mask names with this detection rule pack, applied to session\-derived and
configuration\-derived names alike; a missing or malformed pack exits 6.
